---
import GovLayout from '../../layouts/GovLayout.astro';
---
<GovLayout title="Money Laundering & Criminal Faction" description="Mechanics of the Criminal Faction, Money Laundering, and Police interactions.">
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <span class="govuk-caption-xl">Justice & Law Enforcement</span>
      <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Money Laundering & Criminal Faction</h1>

      <p class="govuk-body-l">
        Delivering illicit cargo allows players to launder money, entering the Criminal Faction and participating in an active cat-and-mouse game with law enforcement.
      </p>

      <div class="govuk-warning-text">
        <span class="govuk-warning-text__icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
        <strong class="govuk-warning-text__text">
          <span class="govuk-warning-text__assistive">Warning</span>
          Participating in these activities puts you at risk of arrest. Police can confiscate <strong>all</strong> of your accumulated illicit earnings if you are caught while Wanted.
        </strong>
      </div>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Illicit Cargo</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        The following cargo types are considered illicit and trigger criminal mechanics when delivered:
      </p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Money / Money Pallet</li>
        <li>Ganja / Ganja Pallet</li>
        <li>Coca Leaves Pallet</li>
        <li>Cocaine</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Money Laundering Mechanics</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Completing illicit deliveries triggers the following effects:
      </p>

      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>Treasury Cost:</strong> Money deliveries deduct 20% of the laundered payment from the public Treasury Fund.</li>
        <li><strong>Criminal Record:</strong> Delivering illicit cargo gives you an active Criminal Record lasting 7 days. Further deliveries reset the 7-day timer.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Criminal Level:</strong> Your level increases with every $50,000 laundered cumulatively.
          Your in-game tag reflects this — <code>[C]</code> at level 1, <code>[C2]</code> at level 2, and so on.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Wanted Status:</strong> Each illicit delivery has a probability of triggering a <strong>Wanted</strong> status.
          The chance scales with the delivery value — from a 5% floor on small deliveries up to 100% for deliveries worth $200,000 or more.
          If a Wanted status is already active, delivering more illicit cargo refreshes it and adds the new payment to your accumulated total.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Wanted Status & Proximity Decay</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        The Wanted system is <strong>permanent</strong> — it does not expire on a timer. Your Wanted level only decreases when on-duty police officers are physically near you.
      </p>

      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>
          <strong>Stars (W1–W5):</strong> Your Wanted level is displayed as 1–5 stars based on your remaining heat.
          All Wanted statuses start at W5 (maximum heat).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Proximity decay (1/r²):</strong> Police presence drains your heat using an inverse-square law.
          A police officer 50m away decays your heat at a rate of 1×/tick.
          At 10m (point-blank), the rate is capped at 10×/tick — clearing full Wanted in roughly 30 seconds.
          Beyond ~200m, the effect is negligible.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Multiple officers:</strong> The nearest on-duty officer determines the decay rate.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Offline safety:</strong> If you log off or no police are on duty, your Wanted status does not decay — it waits until you are online with police present.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Teleporting near police:</strong> Teleporting while Wanted and within 2km of a police officer escalates your heat using the same 1/r² law (up to +300 heat point-blank). This is intended to discourage using teleports to escape arrests.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>When Wanted expires:</strong> Your illicit earnings become "safe" — a server announcement confirms this. No confiscation can occur after expiry.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Arrest & Confiscation</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        While you are Wanted, on-duty police can arrest you. On arrest, your Wanted status is immediately expired and <strong>your full accumulated illicit amount is confiscated</strong> — this is the total of all deliveries recorded on that Wanted record.
      </p>

      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>
          <strong>Auto-arrest:</strong> The patrol system automatically arrests any Wanted suspect who remains within
          <strong>40m of an officer on foot</strong> (or 12m if the officer is in a vehicle) for <strong>4 consecutive seconds</strong>
          while moving slower than 30 km/h. A warning is sent after 1.5 seconds.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Manual arrest (<code>/arrest</code>):</strong> Officers can manually arrest suspects within
          <strong>30m on foot</strong> (or 20m in a police vehicle) over a 3-second verification window.
          The suspect must remain within range and below ~20 km/h throughout.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Arrest zones:</strong> When active arrest zones are configured by admins, arrests may only be made within designated areas.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>On arrest:</strong> The suspect is teleported to jail, the Wanted status is expired, and the full <code>Wanted.amount</code> (all accumulated delivery payments) is confiscated.
          The confiscated amount is split between the Treasury and the arresting officer as a reward.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Wanted = no confiscation:</strong> If a player is arrested without an active Wanted record, no money is taken.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="govuk-body">
        For full details on police progression, confiscation levels, and officer commands, see the <a href="/justice/arrest-wanted" class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state">Arrest &amp; Wanted System</a> documentation.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</GovLayout>
